Common Mistakes
❌ Believing NAT is a firewall.
❌ Thinking every device needs its own public IP address.
❌ Assuming a dynamic IP address changes every time you refresh a webpage.
❌ Confusing DHCP with DNS.
Remember:
•	DHCP assigns IP addresses.
•	DNS translates names into IP addresses.
________________________________________
Memory Tips
NAT
Many private addresses share one public address.
DHCP
Automatically assigns network settings.
Static IP
Stays the same.
Dynamic IP
Assigned automatically and may change.
________________________________________
Self-Assessment
